// Figure 4.10 — System architecture (deployment on one development computer)
// Eraser: New diagram > Cloud architecture, paste this code.
direction right

Users [color: orange] {
  Analyst [icon: user]
  Administrator [icon: user-check]
}

Development computer (Windows 10) [icon: laptop, color: gray] {
  Browser (Edge) [icon: monitor]

  Web tier [color: blue] {
    Next.js 15 web app (port 3000) [icon: nextjs]
  }

  Model tier [color: purple] {
    FastAPI inference (port 8000) [icon: python]
    TensorFlow / Keras CNN [icon: tensorflow]
    Shadow model (optional) [icon: copy]
  }

  Data tier [color: green] {
    PostgreSQL 18 (port 5432) [icon: postgres]
  }

  Files [color: gray] {
    Model bundle folder [icon: folder]
    ULB test split CSV [icon: file]
  }

  Python simulator [icon: send]
  Training pipeline [icon: terminal]
}

Analyst > Browser (Edge)
Administrator > Browser (Edge)
Browser (Edge) <> Next.js 15 web app (port 3000): HTTPS in production / HTTP locally; SSE live updates
Python simulator > Next.js 15 web app (port 3000): POST transactions (API key)
Next.js 15 web app (port 3000) > FastAPI inference (port 8000): /predict, /explain (internal key)
Next.js 15 web app (port 3000) > PostgreSQL 18 (port 5432): SQL (fraud_app role)
FastAPI inference (port 8000) > TensorFlow / Keras CNN
FastAPI inference (port 8000) > Shadow model (optional)
TensorFlow / Keras CNN < Model bundle folder
Training pipeline > Model bundle folder
Training pipeline > ULB test split CSV
Python simulator < ULB test split CSV
